Z||000000||gabriel||02-10-2001||12:27 AM||||Hi guys.<P>  I believe I've seen postings from C. west &/or Will at West Coast Fiero on the forum.  If not, the questions still go out to all.<P>  I've sent querys re. ordering conversion products for the 3800SC swap via email more than once, and have recieved no reply.  That's okay though, maybe I'm just not getting through.<P>  I've read excellent reviews on thier products & support, but have seen concerns re. speed.  Not horsepower -speed of response.<P>  I will be ready to start the install in about two weeks, and really would like to have the mounts & such ready.<P>  Does anyone have any info re. West Coast Fiero's timeline on ordering, & backlog & such?<P>  I would call, but calls from Fl. to California aren't really cheap, & I see no 800#<p>[This message has been edited by gabriel (edited 02-10-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||Sleeper||02-10-2001||01:58 AM||||i've sometimes waited up to two weeks for a email reply so i just call him now, i don't think its his fault though he just gets to busy in the shop. <BR>i know the call will probably be expensive but he does pick-up quick(every time i've called, at least) and plus i don't think he has online ordering so you probably have to call anyways.<P>------------------<BR>85 GT<BR>17" Racing Hart C5 wheels, Kumho Ecsta Supra 712 tires, Intrax lowering spring, KYB shocks, KYB-GR2 struts, Chris West's Strut Tower Bar, J.E.T. super chip, Accel Super Coil, Accel Wires, K&N filter and Optima Battery.||||reg||1
