Z||000005||c m west||02-12-2001||04:20 PM||||Wannabe got it exactly right. It is hard to get back to everyone who emails us here at the shop. But heres the latest info - Will left about 5 months ago due to the fact that he just didnt know a Fiero from a hole in the ground, but dont get me wrong he is still a cool guy. What we do here at the shop is mainly movie props, yacht products, and varius fabrication. The Fiero stuff started out as a hobby that was just making stuff for a few of our buds that had Fieros at the time, but now has exploded into a buisness, one that we would like to devote 100% of our time to, instead of one week 100% and the next 50%. Only with the support of our customers will we be able to do that, and we here at West Coast Fiero thank everyone for thier support this far. As far as phone calls go it is possible to reach us when a customer hasnt allready called in asking questions that could be answered on the shop's web site ( cwestco.com ). So please bare withy us - remember, were here for you guys.<P>Eric Nelson - West Coast Fiero<P>P.S. - the emails will be answered much more frequently ( at least 3 to 4 times a week )<P>||||reg||14
Z||000006||1FST2M6||02-12-2001||04:58 PM||||well since CwestCo os being represented here.. I'll go first..<P>Spoke with Chris in Jan of last year about the Dual intake kit and the rear needle bearing replacement kits. and was told they will be done soon. I bought a set of your Long tube headers and  was wanting the Twin intake kit. what ever became of that. <P>my header install dyno sheet. I had fuel provisions and timing provisions after a couple hours of dyno tuning this is the best we could muster.. the 11lbft loss wasn't worth the 7hp gain.. just my $.02 Chris got this sheet the same day it was dynoed. <BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/2m6headerdyno.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/2m6headerdyno.jpg</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/2m6header1.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/2m6header1.jpg</A> <P>but the bigger the displacement i'm sure the better the HP /  TQ number would be. <P>anywho.. any word on the Twin intake kit and the rear needle bearing replacement sets?<P><BR>Travis Hall<BR>Engineered Performance Inc.<BR>Smyrna, Ga <P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig1fst.jpg">    <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 02-12-2001).]||||reg||1
